---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Prose title="Privacy policy" description={`How ${site.legalName} handles information submitted through this website.`} eyebrow="Legal">
  <p class="draft">
    <strong>Placeholder.</strong> The final privacy policy is supplied by the Owner and reviewed by appropriate advisers
    before launch. The outline below reflects how the site is built, so the final text can be checked against it.
  </p>
  <h2>What this site collects</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Contact and assessment forms: name, work email, organization, and optionally phone and a short message.</li>
    <li>Checklist download: name and work email.</li>
    <li>No file uploads, chat widgets, session recording, or advertising pixels.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>No patient information</h2>
  <p>
    This site is for business inquiries only. Please do not include patient or resident information. If it arrives by
    mistake, access is restricted and it is handled under our incident process.
  </p>
  <h2>Where submissions go</h2>
  <p>Form submissions are delivered to {site.legalName}’s business mailbox. They are not stored by a third-party form vendor.</p>
  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>Cookieless, privacy-first website analytics. To be confirmed against the final configuration before launch.</p>
  <h2>Bookings</h2>
  <p>Discovery calls are booked through Microsoft Bookings, which has its own privacy terms.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about this policy: <a href="/contact">contact us</a>.</p>
</Prose>
